      "caveat": "Every structural variant in the cohort's samples whose gene 1 or gene 2 is one of ALK, ROS1, RET, one row per call as the portal lists them (a patient with several samples carrying the same event has a row for each; a call between two of the genes is listed once). Profiling, panel-aware — ALK: 52 samples with a call, 10,945 of 10,945 profiled; ROS1: 43 samples with a call, 10,945 of 10,945 profiled; RET: 31 samples with a call, 10,945 of 10,945 profiled. A sample not profiled for a gene's structural variants has no row and is not counted as without one. Annotation is OncoKB v7.5's gene-level fusion call (its 'Fusion' entry) for the stronger of the two partners, where its store holds one — not the portal's per-pair fusion annotation; a blank means no call for either gene. Genes 1 and 2 are as the study records the breakpoints (site 1, site 2), not reordered. 131 structural variants. Sorted drivers first, then by gene 1, then gene 2 across the cohort; every page is a slice of that one order, and the download holds every row kept, with every column. ",
